      "hints": [
        "Use the partial-fraction form $\\dfrac{A}{3-x}+\\dfrac{Bx+C}{1+3x^2}$ because the denominator has one linear and one irreducible quadratic factor.",
        "Multiply through by $(3-x)(1+3x^2)$ to obtain $5-x+6x^2=A(1+3x^2)+(Bx+C)(3-x)$.",
        "Equate the constant, $x$ and $x^2$ coefficients, or substitute convenient values, and then insert the three constants into the decomposition."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "State or imply the form $\\frac{A}{3-x}+\\frac{Bx+C}{1+3x^2}$",
        "Use a correct method to find a constant",
        "Obtain one of $A=2$, $B=0$ and $C=1$",
        "Obtain a second value",
        "Obtain the third value",
        "$\\mathrm{f}(x)=\\frac2{3-x}+\\frac1{1+3x^2}$."
